//
// A local bound to a call whose tail is a JOIN — an arm projecting into the callee's
// temporary, another arm a fresh record — releases what it holds when it is rebound, on
// every backend.
//
// @FR-O-Witness: a rebound local frees the value it held; @FR-F-Ret: the callee hands back
// a fresh value.  `pc` answered the projecting arm as a view of its freed temporary
// (loft#2289), so the call read to the ownership oracle as one of several stores with no
// nameable base: `--native`'s rebind tracker learned no owner and `dr = CInt { value: 7 }`
// left the first result behind (`kt=102 CInt×1`, loft#2290).  With the projection copied
// into the caller's buffer the callee answers one store and the rebind releases it.
//
// Axes this file MOVES:  the rebind's source (a literal, the same call); the field type (a
//                        record enum, a struct).
// Axes it HOLDS FIXED:   the arm that RAN is the fresh one — the projecting arm's value is
//                        the F-Ret/2289 cell's channel, kept out of this one so a wrong value
//                        cannot stop the run before the leak report; a dense return; a
//                        straight-line rebind.
//
// The channel is the suite's leak check (`LOFT_LEAK_CHECK=1`, both lanes): a store left at
// exit fails the cell; the printed values are the control.
//
// @falsified-at: a0106bd01 — native exit 0 -> 0 with `1 stores not freed at program exit:
// kt=102 CInt×1` -> clean, scored by hand with a build carrying the defect; interpret clean
// on both trees (the interpreter always freed it).
// HOLDS: the interpreter is clean on both trees, and the answers are equal everywhere.
enum CV { CNull, CInt { value: integer }, CText { value: text } }
struct In { a: integer, t: text }
struct Dec { const value: CV, const next: integer, inn: In }
fn decode(n: integer) -> Dec { Dec { value: CInt { value: n }, next: 1, inn: In { a: n, t: "i{n}" } } }
fn pc(n: integer) -> CV { if n > 0 { decode(n).value } else { CInt { value: 9 } } }
fn pi(n: integer) -> In { if n > 0 { decode(n).inn } else { In { a: 9, t: "z" } } }
fn v(c: CV) -> integer { match c { CInt { value } => value, _ => -1 } }
fn main() {
  dr = pc(0); a = v(dr); dr = CInt { value: 7 };
  f = pc(0); c = v(f); f = pc(0);
  g = pi(0); d = g.a; g = In { a: 6, t: "y" };
  assert("{a} {v(dr)} {c} {v(f)} {d} {g.a}" == "9 7 9 9 9 6", "the values");
  print("2290 a rebound local releases a branch-joined call result ok\n");
}
